# Third-party code

glitter-core's own code is licensed under the Eclipse Public License 2.0
(see LICENSE, Copyright 2026 Burin Choomnuan). The vendored third-party
code keeps the license it came with, which EPL 2.0 does not change. This
file is the authoritative, file-by-file record of what came from where,
and carries the full text of each upstream license, which applies to
those files in addition to glitter-core's own.

Extracted from [jlt-commons/glitter](https://github.com/jlt-commons/glitter):
the toolkit-agnostic two-thirds of that project, split out so a consumer
that never touches GTK4 doesn't have to install it. `glitter` itself now
depends on this package. See glitter's own NOTICE, at the commit this was
extracted from (`75a36e603549b6b4845772c820e719b84ef06586`), for the
complete original record.

## Replicant

The following files are ported from
[Replicant](https://github.com/cjohansen/replicant), commit
`379bb3c1ad4d5d3002c57e67ab647d12f3c2d322` (2026-07-25), by Christian
Johansen. Porting is a mechanical rename (`replicant.*` → `glitter.*`,
including the `:replicant/*` keyword namespace) via
`sed -E 's/\breplicant\b/glitter/g'`, with any further deviation noted in
