## nexus

`src/glitter/nexus/action_log.clj` ports a CONCEPT (not a literal file)
from `nexus.action-log` + `nexus.inspector`
(https://github.com/cjohansen/nexus), commit
`5f6c93672f25d2a5b2a91ac3b65a921ecf8826b2`, by Christian Johansen, Magnar
Sveen, and Teodor Heggelund. MIT License — same terms as the Replicant
bucket above (see that bucket's license block for the full text), under
copyright 2025 Christian Johansen, Magnar Sveen, Teodor Heggelund.

There is no single upstream file to mirror: the log-accumulation logic
lives inside `nexus.inspector` upstream, entangled with `dataspex.*`
rendering-protocol implementations with no glitter/GTK equivalent. This
file ports the accumulation mechanism faithfully (the same nested
`:entries`/`:chronology` tree) and drops every `dp/*`/dataspex call site.
Three adaptations, carried over unchanged from the glitter port: `now`
uses `tick.core/now` instead of `java.util.Date.`; `find-event` reads
`:glitter/dom-event` directly instead of upstream's generic hunt through
`dispatch-data`'s values, since glitter's `dispatch-data` always IS the
event map; `measure-elapsed` returns a plain `{:ms .. :slow? ..}` map
instead of upstream's rounded `Timing` record (`inspector.cljc`'s
`round-tenth`) — a correct adaptation, not an oversight, since `Timing`
is a dataspex render type with no glitter equivalent, simply never
written down until now.

Unlike `nexus.core`/`nexus.registry` (which moved to the standalone
[jlt-commons/nexus-jolt](https://github.com/jlt-commons/nexus-jolt) repo
because nothing in them is glitter-specific), this file's
`:glitter/dom-event` coupling ties it to glitter's own event shape, so it
stays here under its original `glitter.nexus.action-log` name.

## glitter's own code

`src/glitter/env.clj` (glitter's Jolt/GTK-specific environment-detection
helper — not a port of replicant.env, which concerns ClojureScript
compiler presence/optimization, irrelevant to Jolt) and
`src/glitter/test_renderer.clj` (its headless in-memory `IRender`/
`IMemory` fake, inspired by replicant's mutation_log.cljc but separately
implemented) are glitter-core's own new code, EPL 2.0 under the
copyright above — not third-party code, listed here only for
completeness against glitter's own NOTICE, which records the same two
files as "new code specific to glitter."
